						<div class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 uppercase tracking-wide">💡 Key Takeaway</div>
						<div class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300 font-sans mt-0.5">Unbundling term life cover from investments creates substantial wealth arbitrage.</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Card 4: Doubling Money Myth -->
				<div class="faq-card bg-slate-50 dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10 rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-3.5 hover:border-slate-300 dark:hover:border-white/20 transition-all duration-200 ease-geist shadow-xs flex flex-col justify-between" data-category="xirr">
					<div class="space-y-2">
						<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
							<span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-widest bg-rose-100 text-rose-800 dark:bg-rose-950/80 dark:text-rose-300 border border-rose-200 dark:border-rose-800">
								TIME BLINDNESS
							</span>
							<span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400 dark:text-zinc-500 font-semibold">Q04</span>
						</div>
						<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-zinc-100 font-sans leading-snug">
							The agent promised to double my money. Why is the XIRR yield so low?
						</h3>
						<p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-sans">
							Doubling money sounds attractive, but time is the critical variable. Doubling money over 20 years yields only ~3.5% CAGR—which completely loses to 6% inflation. Always judge an investment by XIRR speed, never absolute payouts.
						</p>
